{"case_id":"T5022","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["API protocol","stateful allocation/deallocation","serialization and getter output handling"],"confidence":92,"affected_functions":["plist_mem_free","plist_to_xml","plist_to_bin","plist_get_key_val","plist_get_string_val","plist_get_data_val"],"reason":"H0 only invokes plist_from_bin or plist_from_xml and then plist_free on the resulting tree. It never exercises S1's public allocation/deallocation protocol in which buffers returned by serialization and value-getter APIs must be released with plist_mem_free. This leaves fuzz-derived node types, output sizes, allocation results, NULL outputs, and repeated allocate/free sequences outside sanitizer coverage.","evidence":["S1 adds PLIST_API void plist_mem_free(void* ptr), which conditionally calls free(ptr).","The S1 header explicitly identifies plist_to_xml(), plist_to_bin(), plist_get_key_val(), plist_get_string_val(), and plist_get_data_val() as producers of memory to release through plist_mem_free().","fuzz/bplist_fuzzer.cc only calls plist_from_bin(...) followed by plist_free(root_node).","fuzz/xplist_fuzzer.cc only calls plist_from_xml(...) followed by plist_free(root_node).","Neither H0 target calls plist_mem_free or any listed buffer-producing API."],"recommended_action":"Add a harness path that parses fuzz input, exercises applicable type-specific getters and both serialization functions on successfully created trees, and releases every returned buffer with plist_mem_free, including NULL-safe and repeated operation sequences."}
